// r0z4pb probe (bad): the parameter `r` points into `w` of the handled body. The clause resumes in a nested handled body, the rest ends and frees `w`, then the clause reads `r` (W0301).
effect Tick { fn tick(r: &u64) }
effect Other { fn other() }
fn main() {
    handle Tick { fn tick(r: &u64) {
            handle Other { fn other() { resume(()) } } in { resume(()) }
            print(r + 1)
        } } in {
        let w = Vec.new()
        w.push(5)
        tick(&w[0])
    }
}
